<title>ITALY: Eridania sees better 1997 than 1996.</title>
<headline>Eridania sees better 1997 than 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Europe's largest agribusiness group Eridania Beghin-Say believes that its net result for 1997 will be better than 1996's 1.66 billion french francs, the group chairman Stefano Meloni said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;I hope this year to see results better than last year,&quot; he said, adding that results in the first months of 1997 have pointed towards a positive trend underway. He said sales in 1997 will be closer to 60 billion francs than 55 billion francs.</p>
<p>In 1996, the French-based group which is majority-owned by Italy's Montedison had annual sales of 54.978 billion francs. In the first quarter of 1997, group sales were 14.8 billion francs compared to 13.0 billion francs previously.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
